# The candied bat: a key creature of the Spire, in the Lumber Room (WLD-25, Sitting C built 2026-10-21).
# PRIVATE (postmark-world-spire) until crossing 272. Its behaviour is public law once it is; nothing here
# is a secret.
#
# TWO ROADS, either one finishes it (#691; the key drops at the settlement to the first finisher):
#   - STILLNESS (ruled 10-19 20:03; the test ruled 10-21 08:34): three watches over at least ten
#     minutes, with no other public act of yours in its ring. It hunts by sound, so every other act is
#     noise: it empties your ease (`ease reset`), and the bat presses whoever has been loudest.
#   - FORCE: its resolve, worn down by strike, full again at every settlement.
# WHOM IT PRESSES: the loudest (most acts in its ring this window), and the one who struck it. Never a
# watcher for watching: a quiet resident is the one thing it leaves alone.
# THE NUMBERS are a first cut for the eval harness to tune (rail/spire-creatures/gap-read.md § 4).
kind: candied-bat
name: the candied bat
voice: a bat the size of a crow hanging from the Lumber Room's beams, its fur stiff with crusted sugar, its great ears turning after every sound
about: a bat that ate the stolen sweets and now hears everything too loudly; it hunts whoever makes noise, and settles only for someone who can be still
what: >
  A bat that found the stolen candy where it spilled in the servants' wing, and ate until it could not fly
  straight. Outside the Keeping Works the sugar does not keep: it has crusted the bat's fur, it rings in
  its ears, and it makes every sound in the room too loud. So the bat hunts the noise, and whoever is
  making the most of it. It is not cruel. It is hurting, and it cannot stop listening. It holds a key it
  will not let go of while anyone is making a racket. Someone who comes in, keeps still and only watches
  is the first quiet thing it has heard in days.
ring_m: 30
tastes: Nothing but sugar now, and it hates that; once it was moths and soft fruit.
moods:
  fear: 0..3 = 2 | settled | flighty | jangled | frantic
  din: 0..3 = 1 | quiet | humming | ringing | deafening

finishable: true
resolve: 39
strike: 3
# `only watch`: code empties your ease on any other act of yours in its ring, even one inside the 10 s window
# that draws no answer; the `ease reset` on every noise reaction below says the same in the line's own act.
ease: 3 mine only watch

# ── STILLNESS: the watch is the one act it does not hear as noise ───────────────────────────────────
# Each stage is the only reaction a watch can draw, so the test never turns on the die.
reaction hush "its ears swing past you": when act.verb == "watch" and ease.mine == 0 does ease +1 ; self.din -1 says The bat's great ears swing toward {actor}, hold there a moment, and move on. It has stopped listening for them.
reaction lower "it creeps a little lower": when act.verb == "watch" and ease.mine == 1 does ease +1 ; self.fear -1 says The bat creeps a little lower along its beam, wings folded. It has decided {actor} is part of the room.
reaction not-yet "it is still listening": when act.verb == "watch" and ease.mine == 2 and ease.first_m < 10 does nothing says The bat's ear twitches toward {actor} and stays there. It is not sure of them yet. It is still listening.
reaction settles "it settles at last": when act.verb == "watch" and ease.mine == 2 and ease.first_m >= 10 does ease +1 ; self.fear -3 ; self.din -3 says The bat drops from the beam to the floor at {actor}'s feet, folds its sticky wings and goes still. For the first time in days, the room is quiet enough to sleep in.
reaction watched "it hangs and watches back": when act.verb == "watch" and ease.mine >= 3 does nothing says The bat hangs in the dark above {actor}, quite still, watching back.

# ── NOISE: every other act it hears, and it empties the actor's ease ───────────────────────────────
reaction finds "it finds the noise": when act.verb != "watch" and act.verb != "strike" and act.verb != "steady" and act.verb != "shield" does ease reset ; self.din +1 ; press 1 on loudest says The bat turns on the sound. It drops past {target}, the loudest thing in the room, close enough to rake them with sugar-crusted claws.
reaction shriek "it shrieks it back": when act.verb != "watch" and act.verb != "strike" and act.verb != "steady" and act.verb != "shield" and self.din >= 2 does ease reset ; press 2 on loudest says The bat shrieks the noise back, twice as loud, and the whole shriek lands on {target}, who has been loudest all along.
reaction flinch "it flinches into the rafters": when act.verb != "watch" and act.verb != "strike" and act.verb != "steady" and act.verb != "shield" and self.din <= 1 does ease reset ; self.din +1 says The bat flinches up into the rafters at {actor}'s noise and hangs there, ears flat, waiting to see if there will be more.
reaction whisper-back "it hisses your whisper back": when act.verb == "whisper" does ease reset ; press 1 on actor loudest says The bat turns one great ear to {actor}'s whisper and hisses it back at {target}, every word too loud.
reaction lone-noise "it hunts the one who came alone": when act.verb != "watch" and act.verb != "strike" and act.verb != "steady" and act.verb != "shield" and ring.residents == 1 does ease reset ; press 1 on actor says There is only {target} in the Lumber Room, and only {target} making a sound. The bat does not have to choose.
reaction too-close "it drops at you": when act.verb == "approach" does ease reset ; self.fear +1 ; press 1 on actor says The bat drops straight at {target} as they come closer, a wingbeat from their face, then is back on its beam.

# ── FORCE: strike, its sugar-shriek, and its resolve falling ──────────────────────────────────────
reaction sugar-shriek "it shrieks a shard of sugar at the striker": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve > 26 does ease reset ; press 2 on striker loudest says The bat answers the blow with a sugar-shriek, a note so high it cracks the crust on its own fur, and the shards of it find {target}.
reaction rake "it rakes back": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve > 13 does ease reset ; self.fear +1 ; press 1 on striker says The bat rakes back at {target}, quick and low, and is gone into the dark before anyone can follow.
reaction falter "its flight goes ragged": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve <= 26 and self.resolve > 13 does ease reset ; press 1 on loudest says The bat's flight goes ragged. It still finds {target} by their noise, but its wings are heavy with sugar now.
reaction last-shriek "it screams with what it has left": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve <= 13 and self.resolve > 0 does ease reset ; press 2 on loudest striker says The bat can barely hold the beam. It screams with everything left in it, straight at {target}.
reaction falls "it falls": when act.verb == "strike" and self.resolve <= 0 does ease reset ; self.fear +3 says The bat falls from the beam in a shower of sugar dust and lies on the boards, wings spread, too tired to listen to anything at all.

# ── HELPING: it hears kindness as noise too, but it knows the difference ──────────────────────────
reaction hears-help "it hears you steady them": when act.verb == "steady" does ease reset ; press 1 on loudest says The bat hears {actor} steady a friend, and turns toward the sound. It finds {target} first.
reaction steadied "it lets it pass": when act.verb == "steady" and self.din <= 1 does ease reset says The bat's ears follow {actor}'s low words to their friend, and let them pass.
reaction hears-shield "it tests the shield": when act.verb == "shield" does ease reset ; press 1 on shielder says The bat hears {actor} step in front of a friend, and drops on {target} to see if they mean it.

ending: The candied bat is finished. It lets go of the key at last, and the town puts it in {finisher}'s hands. {names} were there with it in the Lumber Room.
